  "scientific_conclusion": "Package 171-R7 demonstrated flawless monotonic active-set contraction: zero nodes were added back across the entire simulation (13,803 -> 160 active nodes, a 98.84% reduction), and KKT stationarity was fully satisfied (< 3e-7). However, coupled nonconvergence occurred because Stage 2 acceleration (omega_d = 0.85) was never triggered. The transition threshold (|Delta A_k| <= 2 for 3 iterations) was mathematically over-stringent: in the tail, shedding proceeded at 4-7 nodes/iter (0.025%-0.045% of mesh), reaching |Delta A_k| = 4 at outer 100. Recalibrating to a compound criterion (|A_k| <= 500 AND |Delta A_k| <= 10 for N=3, with zero added nodes) activates Stage 2 at Outer 82, granting 18-38 iterations of accelerated fixed-point relaxation to drive delta_d below 1e-5."
